<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    DWARF register locals, inlined-subroutine locals and parameter storage
    (`option dwarfscopes on|off`), ida95-57.

    Stage P1 external-refinement. dwarfregs_x86_64.c built with gcc -O2 -g:
    `hash` keeps `h` in EAX (a location list), and the inlined `mix` keeps its
    `t` and `u` in EDX/EAX inside a DW_TAG_inlined_subroutine.
    dwarfregparm_i386.c built with gcc -m32 -O2 -g: `combine` is
    `regparm(3)`, so DWARF puts `a`, `b`, `c` in EAX, EDX, ECX at entry while
    the default i386 model expects them on the stack.

    Pass 1 (`dwarfscopes off`, the bug): register-held locals are anonymous, and
    `combine` reads three uninitialized registers while its caller passes stack
    garbage. Pass 2 (default, the fix): the locals carry their DWARF names and
    `combine` takes its parameters in the registers DWARF states, at the
    definition and at the call.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x100000" readonly="true">
c3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x100000" name="harness_stub"/>
</binaryimage>
